    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 29 with a clear mandate: exploit speed and favorable pitching matchups to stabilize our Roto standing. The anchor of today\u2019s lineup is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who commands our highest score. Facing Canning, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an elite +14% platoon edge and a +14% SP skill bump, making him our primary engine for both runs and the stolen base category. **Yordan Alvarez** (71.16) follows closely behind, as his xwOBA of 0.444 against Matthews suggests he is the most likely candidate to provide high-ceiling HR and RBI production, effectively neutralizing the slight park disadvantage. Additionally, **Caleb Durbin** (66.81) earns a high-leverage start due to the aggressive base-running environment created by Mikolas\u2019s slow delivery, which significantly boosts his scoring projection in our SB-heavy model.\n\nThe platoon dynamics are central to our construction today, specifically with **Carson Benge** (64.91), who leverages a strong +7% platoon advantage against Yesavage to anchor the top of the order. Conversely, the most difficult decision involved **Gary Sanchez** (55.71); while he maintains a solid score, he hovered near the marginal threshold due to the threat posed by Lodolo. **Gary Sanchez** ultimately secured the start over potential bench options because of his sustained recency weighting and the high-leverage context of his order position. We are closely monitoring the status of **Trea Turner** (55.69) and **Kyle Schwarber** (53.95); while both are starting, the pairing against Ashcraft remains a risk, as the SP skill adjustment drags their scores down by 15%. We remain prepared to shift focus to our bench depth\u2014including **Lars Nootbaar** or **Luke Raley**\u2014should any last-minute weather reports or late-scratch notifications force a tactical pivot.",
